{
  "name": "three boards in a row, the middle one turned round, signal as one",
  "covers": [
    "track numbering at a joint, with one board turned round"
  ],
  "about": "Three copies of one double-track module. On each, North Home stands at end A and signals trains going towards end B on its north line (track 2 of end A, track 1 of end B); South Home stands at end B and signals the other way on its south line (track 2 of end B, track 1 of end A). Each block includes what the far end hears on that line, and each mast reads the next mast there. West and east face the same way; mid is turned round, so west's B meets mid's B and mid's A meets east's A, and mid's south line carries the eastbound trains. Track 1 meets the far end's last track, so west's North Home reads mid's South Home, which reads east's North Home: Clear, Clear, Approach before the end of the line. A train on that line drops them in turn, and the boundary sensor at mid's South Home holds west's block too; the other line is never touched. A train on mid's north line (eastbound's other line) reaches only east's South Home. Mid losing the broker sends its neighbours' masts facing it to Stop until it is back.",
